    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d190">

                <pb facs="0438" n="406" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v19/pg406"/>

                <head>190. Telegram From the Embassy in Poland to the
                        Department of State<anchor n="0" xml:id="d190-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Warsaw</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1958-10-15T19:00:00+01:00">October 15, 1958,
                            7 p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>596. USUN for Lodge. Beam–Wang Talks. 81st meeting two hours 15
                        minutes.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d190-f2"/></p>
                <p>I led off with prepared statement based on Deptel 440.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d190-f3"/></p>
                <pb facs="0439" n="407" xml:id="pg407"/>
                <p>Wang replied with point by point rejection both US draft
                    agreed announcements arguing they were simply devices to legalize US
                    “occupation” Taiwan and carry out “two-Chinas plot”. Again drew careful
                    distinction between Chinese internal affairs which he declared not fit subject
                    for discussion these talks and presence and preparations of US forces in the
                    area on which he insisted discussion should be centered. Said if US sincerely
                    interested reaching peaceful settlement through negotiation we should begin
                    discussion on basis ChiComs September 22
                        [proposal].<anchor n="3" xml:id="d190-f4"/></p>
                <p>I attacked Wang’s distinction between internal and
                    international aspects of situation using material last paragraph for total US
                    capitulation and again asked for evidence ChiCom desire reach peaceful settlement through genuine
                    negotiation.</p>
                <p>Using material from Secretary’s press conference<anchor n="4" xml:id="d190-f5"/>
                    Wang challenged US competence discuss such matters as force
                    strength on offshore islands and again questioned authority US represent GRC. I
                    replied along lines last paragraph Deptel
                        451.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d190-f6"/> In subsequent give and take
                        Wang attacked GRC and US relationship thereto while I
                    refuted his arguments.</p>
                <p>I proposed next meeting Monday, Wang countered with
                    Wednesday October 22, 2 p.m. Thereupon I proposed Thursday October 23, 2 p.m.
                    which Wang accepted.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Beam</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
